From e0d84419c61d65a78170c5f528804311887fcb58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DSH deployment <dsh-deployment@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:13:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(deepseek-harness): replace Caddy with plain-HTTP
 Node proxy

- drop Caddy, TLS, internal CA and basic auth: the container now serves
  plain HTTP on 8080 and expects an authenticated TLS reverse proxy in front
- add node-proxy.mjs: Host allowlist, security headers, JSON access log,
  /healthz, optional shared secret, WebSocket passthrough, streaming, 502/504
- entrypoint: remove username/password validation and argon2 hashing, keep
  uid/gid fixups, readiness wait, --trusted-host and the DSH auth bypass patch
- keep DSH_ACCESS_HOST (HTTPS_ACCESS_HOST accepted with deprecation warning)
- tests: replace the Caddy test with 14 proxy tests
- release workflow: publish the plain-HTTP variant to its own repository
  (1panel/deepseek-harness-plain) instead of overwriting the Caddy image tags
